Source-side drag selection loss (2026-10-25)
============================================

- Treat loss of the Motif drag selection as a terminal ownership event. An
  active pointer drag is cancelled immediately; a pointer-complete drop that
  is still awaiting transfer completion is finished with failure. This retires
  the drag context once instead of leaving later conversion or timeout work
  pointed at a source that no longer owns the selection.
- Add owner-replacement and post-drop incremental-transfer installed probes.
  Three fresh AArch64 Xvfb runs pass 8 checks for active owner replacement and
  14 checks for post-drop cancellation in each run. The existing same-process,
