Xt selection-context lifetime dependency patch (2026-10-25)
=============================================================

- Extend the pinned libXt 1.3.1 patch with a lookup-only disown path and
  guarded context retirement: a widget-destroy callback removes an inactive
  context immediately, active transfers retire it at their final reference,
  and `XtDisownSelection` clears the X selection owner only when that widget
  still owns it.  The patch also clears the final INCR value pointer after Xt
  frees it.  This keeps the existing Xt/Motif API and callback order.
- The official dependency build helper and a fresh AArch64 installed-prefix
  run pass ABI, `incremental-layout` and `clipboard-lifetime` under strict
  ASan/UBSan leak detection.  Broader Fontconfig, application drag-and-drop
  and cross-architecture ownership gates remain explicitly separate.

Native dependency-runner propagation (2026-10-25)
==================================================

- Propagate repeated `--runtime-library-dir` arguments into the local Compose
  observer and record them in its receipt. The normal installed-prefix local
  XIM/XIC fixture now proves that the pinned external Xt is loaded instead of
  silently falling back to system Xt. Strict execution reaches the fixture
  body but remains bounded by the external Fontconfig ownership report; no
  leak suppression was added.
- When a strict child exits before its final protocol response, retain its
  exit status and stderr tail in the observer failure instead of reporting a
  racy EOF with no ownership evidence.

Virtual-keycode range guard (2026-10-25)
========================================

- Guard `XmTranslateKey` against keycodes outside the server's current X11
  keymap before indexing the Xt keysym table. The guard caches the display
  keycode range during XmDisplay initialization, so valid key translation does
  not add a per-event round trip. A strict installed local-Compose run and a
  focused invalid-boundary consumer pass on a fresh AArch64 prefix.

Native text-fixture Fontconfig teardown (2026-10-25)
=====================================================

- Release the process-global Fontconfig configuration in the layout and
  line-context consumers after their Xft fonts and displays are closed. Strict
  sanitizer results now distinguish consumer teardown from the toolkit's
  remaining external ownership boundary without disabling leak detection.

XLibre shell observer teardown (2026-10-25)
============================================

- Remove the RandR observer's destroy callback when an application explicitly
  unregisters a realized shell, before releasing the observer state. A later
  shell destruction can no longer invoke a freed callback closure. The
  installed observer regression now exercises explicit unregistration and
  post-unregistration destruction.

DataField render-table ownership (2026-10-25)
==============================================

- Free the private render-table copy installed by DataField even when the
  source `XmNfontList` came from the application. The previous provenance flag
  skipped that copy and leaked every Xft rendition in the widget's table.
  The strict Unicode fixture now reaches the separate 104-byte system-Xt
  selection-owner report instead of retaining the toolkit's render tables.

UIL literal-only module output (2026-10-25)
============================================

- Allow `UrmIFMInitModule` to emit a valid empty top-level-widget table for
  UIL modules containing only exported literals and icons.  This fixes the
  full-tree `animate/dog.uil` generation path without changing non-empty
  widget-module layout.  Initialize the first UID index entry when the file
  has no index root, and cover the complete regression with
  `tests/automated/run-uil-zero-topmost.py`.

XLibre live RandR observer (2026-10-25)
========================================

- Extend the opt-in XLibre DPI support from parsing and output selection to a
  shell-boundary observer. RandR screen/output/property notifications are
  drained on the owning Xt thread, coalesced into one work procedure, and
  applied through one resize plus a documented derived-metric change hook;
  ordinary X11/Xorg builds remain unchanged. A real multi-output XLibre
  session is still required for the final live qualification gate.
- Extend the installed observer regression to two realized shells sharing one
  Xt display. It verifies descendant lookup, idempotent registration, and
  retirement of one shell without invalidating the surviving shell; ordinary
  Xvfb continues to exercise the explicit fallback path.

Native dependency-cohort qualification (2026-10-25)
====================================================

- Allow the native feature runner to receive explicit additional runtime/link
  library directories for a pinned Xt/X11 dependency cohort. The selected
  Motif prefix remains authoritative for `libXm`; every extra directory is
  recorded in the receipt so system-library failures are distinguished from
  toolkit results. The native text/IME matrix documents the interrupted
  clipboard-transfer boundary.

The XLibre contract runner now executes its shell observer on the supplied
real display, checking registration and scale lookup there; its Xvfb path
continues to require ordinary-server fallback.
The fixture also checks that unrealized shells are never registered and that
ordinary-server scale lookup falls back cleanly.
Descendant lookup is covered by the same shell-boundary fixture.

Transfer-storage dependency cohort (2026-10-25)
================================================

- Extend `run-storage-regressions.py` with repeatable focused modes and
  explicit additional runtime/link library directories. The receipt records
  the selected dependency cohort, and the clipboard, merge, bounds and owner
  lifetime modes pass against the pinned corrected Xt on AArch64. This does
  not promote the separate Xt callback-lifetime, drag-and-drop or application
  workflow gates to toolkit acceptance.

