Native Unicode hard lines, geometry and retained output (2026-10-24)
====================================================================

- Recognize complete CRLF and mandatory Unicode hard-line separators in native
  UTF-8 source scans/counts without modifying stored bytes or scalar positions.
  Cross whole terminators during visual motion and restart wrapped line-table
  reflow at the current hard paragraph after accepted edits. This prevents an
  old line start inside a newly formed CRLF from being shaped across paragraphs.
  Custom scanners and non-UTF-8 native source policies remain distinct.
- Treat NODELTA as geometry invalidation, retiring cached captures instead of
  adding LONG_MAX to source positions during source replacement or resize.
- Honor explicitly supplied width/height during font changes even when equal to
  current dimensions; derive omitted dimensions from rows/columns independently.
  Refresh global and visible line geometry before cursor/IM queries and native
  navigator notifications, using current font state after callbacks.
- Add independently retained immutable output captures and saturating counters
  of actual paragraph analysis, HarfBuzz shaping and line capture work. Internal
  opaque objects change; existing widget records and ABI epoch 8 stay unchanged.
- Add the incremental-layout native regression: shared sources, retained/rebased
  unaffected captures, mandatory separators, CRLF joins/splits, distant bidi
  context, wrap/font/configuration changes, dimension authority and auto sizing.
  Compare real native output against fresh widgets for source ranges, glyphs,
  wrapping, carets, hits, selections and actual glyph pixels. Include incremental
  source-map/widget/layout fixtures in source distribution metadata.
- Normal AArch64 qualification passes all 33 selected native fixtures. The new
  regression passes 12,890,100 assertions/417 native-fresh line comparisons with
  zero layout warnings; negative controls expose the prior faults. It measures
  reuse of unaffected hard paragraphs, not incremental shaping within an edited
  paragraph or complete interactive editor/input acceptance.
- An earlier strict ASan/UBSan profile reported 208 bytes in two Xt
  selection-context allocations. The pinned dependency patch now closes that
  bounded context path; a separate strict font-lifetime fixture passes 79
  assertions across two displays, zero X errors. An additional strict legacy
  layout probe reports Fontconfig allocations, so broad sanitizer acceptance
  is not claimed. No suppression or disabled leak detection is used. See
  docs/status.md and docs/unicode.md for qualification.

