Appearance display-state lifetime (2026-10-25)
==============================================

- Release cloned appearance Xrm databases with the existing Motif display
  destruction path, and correct Xrm database enumeration semantics so profile
  selection remains reliable for every application resource set.

Appearance transaction reentrancy (2026-10-25)
===============================================

- Reject nested `XmApplyAppearanceProfile` and `XmSetAppearanceProfile` calls
  from a widget `SetValues` hook while a live appearance transaction is in
  progress. The per-display guard prevents interleaved Xrm snapshots while
  preserving the outer transaction's resource and widget state; the installed
  consumer fixture exercises both nested paths under Xvfb.

Appearance transaction atomicity (2026-10-25)
==============================================

- Prepare all profile-owned conversions before committing any widget values,
  retaining one conversion result per widget. A Linux fault-injection
  consumer verifies that staging allocation failure leaves the selected
  profile and realized resources unchanged, then permits a later transition.

Live appearance gadget coverage (2026-10-25)
=============================================

- Register cache-backed Motif gadgets in the live appearance transaction,
  defer their first value snapshot until the gadget cache is initialized, and
  prune destroyed gadgets by parent-manager membership because gadgets do not
  have a normal widget destroy callback. The installed `PushButtonGadget`
  fixture covers explicit-resource preservation, destruction, replacement and
  consumer ASan/UBSan execution.

Display-scale transaction rollback (2026-10-25)
===============================================

- Restore the previous display-scale override when transaction staging cannot
  allocate its callback snapshot, for both setting and clearing an override.
  The installed fault-injection consumer verifies the rollback contract.

Live appearance profile transaction (2026-10-25)
================================================

- Add the additive `XmApplyAppearanceProfile` API. It applies the existing
  classic, modern-light, modern-dark and high-contrast profiles to a realized
  core-widget hierarchy without changing the Xt resource model or explicit
  application values.
- Track profile-owned values separately from explicit widget arguments and
  ordinary X resources, preserve widget state/callbacks, and preflight color
  conversion before committing a transaction. See
  `docs/appearance-profiles.md` and
  `tests/automated/run-live-appearance.py`.

